// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b7-b74
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
assessment "b7.omop" source="b7" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b710.1" source="b710" target="SNOMED_CT:364564000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b710 SNOMED CT 364564000 = ICF b710: the body functions of JOINT MOBILITY — the
        mobility/range of motion of joints (per WHO ICF definition), with children b7100 mobility of
        single joint, b7101 mobility of several joints, b7102 mobility generalized, b7108/b7109
        residuals. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT observable that names the
        range of joint movement as the GENERAL joint-mobility concept (it is the IS_A parent of the
        joint-specific ROM observables: 298773006 shoulder, 298878008 elbow, 298946001 wrist, 299062003
        finger, 404979006 neck, etc. — 14 joint-specific children verified in the ancestors mirror).
        This is the closest standard equivalent and matches the ICF joint-mobility scope at the general
        level. Broader rather than exact: ICF b710 is a multi-child function block (b7100-b7109)
        bundling single-joint, multi-joint AND generalized mobility where is a single observable for the
        range of joint movement; the target names the central joint-ROM axis but does not subsume the
        generalized-mobility / multi-joint-pattern sub-functions, so it stands broader as the single
        best umbrella for the block. High tier : direct term-and-scope match (range of joint movement =
        joint mobility functions) verified active in the mirror with confirmed
        parent-of-joint-specific-ROM hierarchy, one-level-broader in model granularity, no independent
        Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b710-b729.1" source="b710-b729" target="SNOMED_CT:106029005" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b710-b729 SNOMED CT 106029005 = ICF block b710-b729 Functions of the joints and bones: the
        block-level grouping of joint-mobility functions (b710), joint-stability functions (b715),
        skeletal-mobility functions (b720) and the b729 residual. Target =, active RF2 production. No
        single SNOMED CT observable exists; the nearest standard ancestor that contains the joint-mobility,
        joint-stability and skeletal-mobility axes together is the general musculoskeletal-function
        observable. Broader (low): a block-level joint-and-bone grouping mapped up to the whole
        musculoskeletal function is a deeper climb than the b710 block map, and the target subsumes far
        more (muscle tone, muscle power, etc.) than the joint/bone block — but it is the nearest
        defensible ancestor. Per the chapter/block precedent the
        moderate-or-lower tier applies; low chosen because the target is markedly broader than the
        source block. mapping_type=broader.
        """
}
mapping "b7100.1" source="b7100" target="SNOMED_CT:364564000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b7100 SNOMED CT 364564000 = ICF b7100 Mobility of SINGLE joint functions: the specific
        function of the range of movement of one individual joint. Target =, active RF2 production, the
        SNOMED CT observable for joint range of movement. No dedicated function-observable exists in the
        mirror (the active/passive range concepts 786071002/830146005 are measurement observables, and
        33836004 is the broader function-framed parent covering the whole MSK system, not one joint).
        Broader rather than exact: 364564000 is the generic joint-range observable where the source is
        specifically the function of ONE joint (a more specific framing), so the target subsumes the
        source; and 364564000 is a range/measurement observable whereas ICF b7100 is the function
        framing. Low tier : best available specific joint-movement observable, term-verified active, but
        real semantic gap between the ICF single-joint function framing and the SNOMED CT generic
        range-of-joint-movement observable. mapping_type=broader.
        """
}
mapping "b7101.1" source="b7101" target="SNOMED_CT:364564000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b7101 SNOMED CT 364564000 = ICF b7101 Mobility of SEVERAL joints functions: the specific
        function of the range of movement of multiple joints together. Target =, active RF2 production.
        No dedicated function-observable exists in the mirror; 364564000 (range of joint movement,
        generic) is the nearest standard concept and 33836004 (Musculoskeletal mobility, function) is
        the broader MSK function parent. Broader: the generic joint-range observable subsumes the
        several-joints framing; and the measurement-observable vs function framing gap applies as for
        b7100. Low tier : best available joint-movement observable, term-verified active, but the ICF
        several-joints function framing has no exact SNOMED CT analogue. mapping_type=broader.
        """
}
mapping "b7102.1" source="b7102" target="SNOMED_CT:33836004" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b7102 SNOMED CT 33836004 = ICF b7102 General joint mobility functions: the function of joint
        mobility considered generally across the body. Target =, active RF2 production, the
        function-framed SNOMED CT observable for generalised musculoskeletal mobility — the direct
        function-framed match for ICF's general-joint-mobility framing. This is the closest standard
        equivalent; no dedicated observable exists, but 33836004 names MSK mobility AS A FUNCTION
        (matching ICF's function perspective) at the general level. Broader rather than exact: 33836004
        spans the whole MSK system (muscles + joints + bones) where the source is specifically the
        general JOINT mobility axis; the target fully contains the source but adds the muscle/bone
        mobility axes. Moderate tier : direct function-and-scope match (general MSK mobility function),
        term-verified active, but one-level-broader (muscle/bone axes added) and no independent Athena
        crosswalk re-verified. mapping_type=broader.
        """
}
