        mapping a function code to a disorder finding would conflate capacity with pathology. Broader:
        the general muscle-function observable is the nearest defensible function-framed ancestor; the
        source's one-limb specificity is lost (the limb-weakness findings were rejected as
        disorder-framed). Low tier : the only defensible function-framed muscle ancestor, term-verified
        active, but a deeper climb (whole-muscle function vs one-limb power) and the regional
        specificity is sacrificed to avoid a disorder-finding conflation. mapping_type=broader.
        """
}
